.TH "CITADEL" "1" "Sep 2026" "AceTeam" "Citadel CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
citadel-egress-relay-allow-lan - Allow (or deny) the relay CONNECTing into this node's own LAN/mesh


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcitadel egress-relay allow-lan  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
By default the relay refuses to CONNECT to RFC1918 private addresses,
loopback, link-local, and the 100.64.0.0/10 CGNAT/mesh range -- an authorized
peer can egress to the public internet through this node but cannot pivot
into this node's own LAN or mesh. 'allow-lan on' disables that deny-list.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for allow-lan


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug output

.PP
\fB--no-auto-update\fP[=false]
	Disable automatic update checks and installs for this run (or set CITADEL_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable colorized output

.PP
\fB--node-dir\fP=""
	Override the node config directory (citadel.yaml + services/), bypassing $HOME/ConfigDir resolution. Also settable via CITADEL_NODE_DIR. Scope: manifest/services resolution only -- does NOT redirect network state, the module lockfile, or nodevault.

.PP
\fB--runtime\fP=""
	Container runtime for module containers: docker or podman (default: auto-detect)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcitadel-egress-relay(1)\fP
